    <article class="article-wrap">
      <h2>1. High-Level Structural Overview: 7th CPC vs. 8th CPC</h2>
      <p>
        The debate over the <strong>7th vs. 8th Central Pay Commission (CPC)</strong> marks a defining transition for more than 4.8 million central government employees and over 6.7 million pensioners. Every decade, India's public sector compensation shifts from an aging baseline to an updated framework designed to reflect modern cost-of-living metrics, consumption baskets, and economic growth.
      </p>
      <p>
        The transition from the 7th to the 8th Pay Commission involves more than just higher take-home pay. It fundamentally recalibrates basic wage structures, allowance trigger thresholds, pension parity formulas, and entry-level minimum earnings.
      </p>

      <div class="table-responsive">
